cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "capex-atlas: source-linked models of hyperscaler capital deployment"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that turns SEC filings into reproducible models of capital
  deployment, cash flow and returns on invested capital for hyperscale cloud and
  infrastructure operators. Every published figure carries its formula, its
  assumptions and a citation to a primary source, and an evidence status that
  distinguishes reported values from derived, estimated and scenario ones. A
  capital-vintage engine models the lag between capital spending, capacity coming
  into service and depreciation beginning, and inverts the usual question: rather
  than estimating a return from inputs no company discloses, it computes what
  utilization, pricing, margin or delay would have to hold for a stated claim to
  be true.
type: software
authors:
